Erich Owens <[redacted]>
2026-05-20 23:01:36 -0700
fix(claim-tree-viz): empty-page crash + tooltip clipping + sunburst contrast

Empty-page crash:
  d3.select(g).selectAll('[data-node="1"]').data(nodes, d => d.id) was
  running its keyfn against existing DOM elements with no __data__ bound.
  d was undefined, d.id threw, React unmounted the whole subtree.
  Replaced with native React pointer handlers (onPointerDown/Move/Up)
  using a useRef drag state and SVG-coord math.

Treemap + Gantt tooltips:
  Edge-detect: if the cell sits near the top of the SVG, flip the
  tooltip below the cell rather than rendering above and clipping.

Sunburst contrast at root focus:
  Unclaimed directory rings used var(--surface-raised) at 0.4 opacity —
  effectively invisible against the page background. Now use soft
  oklch tints with full opacity so the ring structure is visible even
  when claim coverage is sparse. Smaller centerR (44px) gives the rings
  more room. Visible stroke on every arc.

Force-directed: kept d3.zoom for pan/scroll-to-zoom; replaced d3.drag
with React pointer handlers.


